<title>UK: UK govt approves BAe, Lagardere jv.</title>
<headline>UK govt approves BAe, Lagardere jv.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Trade and Industry Secretary Ian Lang said on Friday that he has approved the planned merger of the guided missile businessses of British Aerospace Plc and France's Lagardere SCA.  </p>
<p>BAe is to merge its missile operations, BAe Dynamics, with the Matra arm of Lagardere. Matra BAe Dynamics will be Europe's largest missile maker, with annual sales of around $1.5 billion.</p>
<p>BAe Defence chief executive John Weston said on Wednesday that the joint venture should be operational before the end of the year, pending regulatory approvals.</p>
<p>News earlier this week that the French government wants to sell electronics giant Thomson SA to Lagardere has raised the prospect of an even larger grouping, which will aim to take on major U.S. missile companies on equal terms.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
